"""Regression tests for the fail-closed safety contract.

Three related audit findings:

1. LLMResponse error contract: every error return from LLMClient sets
   is_error=True with a machine-readable error_type, so callers can fail
   closed without pattern-matching bracketed strings in content.
2. Core agents fail closed on LLM failure: a transport/budget error must
   never flow into JSON parsing as a benign non-answer. Sentinel refuses
   (premise_valid=False), voters dissent; parse failures on REAL model
   output still degrade gracefully (two-way split).
3. Challenge/vote dispatch gates: Phases 2 and 3 pass the same
   identity/suspension/rate-limit/scope gates as Phase 1, so an agent
   suspended mid-run is excluded from later phases and consensus math
   handles the shrinking voter set. Any vote-phase gate-out flags the
   result degraded -- a shrunken denominator is never silent.
4. Error responses never launder content downstream: the enforcement
   rewrite treats an errored call as no-rewrite (rejected stays
   rejected), and synthesis never surfaces the error string as the
   recommended direction.
5. Failure classification trusts the is_error contract when present;
   the legacy prefix check applies only to duck-typed clients without
   the attribute, so a live reply quoting a bracketed error string is
   not misclassified.
"""

import json

import pytest

from {{project_slug}}.agents.capability import AgentCapability
from {{project_slug}}.agents.core import (
    CitationAgent,
    EvidenceAgent,
    FactCheckerAgent,
    QualityAgent,
    SentinelAgent,
    SkepticAgent,
)
from {{project_slug}}.agents.registry import AgentRegistry
from {{project_slug}}.llm.client import LLMClient, LLMResponse
from {{project_slug}}.orchestration.round_table import (
